{"agent_id":"pp3g-H4RK-read-only-mechanism-verification-no-file-changes-no","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-06T05:45:50.937382989Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ae626387-2d74-45ed-b6fa-91d1f44a9b70","comment_uuid":"bff881c2-c4e7-41f3-a786-1028ab271280","author":"pp3g-H4RK-read-only-mechanism-verification-no-file-changes-no","content":"VERDICT (#142 mechanism verification, read-only). Source: /home/claude-code/projects/crosslink @ crosslink/src. Live evidence: ASES main repo + this worktree, 2026-08-06. NOTHING WAS MODIFIED in the crosslink fork or in ASES.\n\n== HEADLINE ==\nHydration has TWO sources, selected structurally (never by config). The v3 source (RefHubSource over refs) is correct and ref-pinned. The rollback comes from the SECOND, v2 source: `maybe_auto_hydrate` runs the v2 worktree-file path on EVERY command with NO hub-mode gate, keyed on the hub-cache worktree HEAD. In ASES/tripn-astro that HEAD is `refs/heads/crosslink/hub`, whose tree still holds the 4 June-era `issues/*.json`, and whose tip MOVES every few minutes because trust key-registration commits land on the checked-out branch. Every tip move invalidates the marker and re-imports the June baseline, dropping every agent-authored row.\n\n== Q1: WHAT REF DOES HYDRATION ACTUALLY READ? ==\nNeither \"hub\" nor \"checkpoint\" alone — it is mode-routed, and one route ignores refs entirely.\n\n(a) v3 route — refs only, worktree-independent.\n- `RefHubSource::new` (hub_source.rs:464) resolves and PINS: `hub_v3::CHECKPOINT_REF` = `refs/heads/crosslink/checkpoint` (hub_v3.rs:45), `hub_v3::META_REF` = `refs/heads/crosslink/meta` (hub_v3.rs:49, trust store only), and every `refs/heads/crosslink/agents/*` (`AGENT_REF_PREFIX`, hub_v3.rs:37).\n- Reads are `git cat-file` against those pinned SHAs: `read_checkpoint` -> `<checkpoint_sha>:state.json` (hub_source.rs:551-570); `read_events` -> `<agent_tip>:events.log` (hub_source.rs:516-549). The hub-cache HEAD / working tree is IRRELEVANT here; the dir is used only as a git repo handle (shared ref namespace via the linked worktree, sync/core.rs:57-62).\n- Effective source = checkpoint (genesis + watermark) PLUS all agent-ref events above that watermark, combined by `compaction::reduce`, then `hydration::hydrate_from_state` (hydration.rs:310).\n- Callers: `sync_cmd` (locks_cmd.rs:263-266), `compact::run` (compact.rs:46-48), `SharedWriter::hydrate_with_retry` when v3 (shared_writer/core.rs:204-219), daemon v3 tick (daemon.rs:20-23 + 276-277), `integrity hydration --repair` on v3 (integrity_cmd.rs:130-133, 335-336), migrate adopt (migrate_hub_v3.rs:182-185).\n\n(b) v2 route — the CHECKED-OUT hub-cache worktree files.\n- `hydration::hydrate_to_sqlite` (hydration.rs:122) reads `<hub-cache>/issues/*.json` (+ `meta/counters.json`, `meta/milestones*`) straight off disk, i.e. whatever branch the hub-cache worktree happens to have checked out.\n- Callers: `sync_v2_readonly` (locks_cmd.rs:303), daemon non-v3 (daemon.rs:279), `integrity hydration --repair` non-v3 (integrity_cmd.rs:378-379), `migrate.rs:262`, tui/mod.rs, `SharedWriter::hydrate_with_retry` non-v3 (shared_writer/core.rs:220-234), and — CRITICALLY — `maybe_auto_hydrate` (hydration.rs:1214) with NO mode check.\n\n(c) The switch: `HubMode::resolve` (hub_v3.rs:709) -> `detect_hub_version` (hub_v3.rs:596) -> `classify_hub_version` (hub_v3.rs:659): meta+checkpoint present => V3, else v2 branch present => V2Only, else Absent(=>V2). Purely structural (ref presence), decided once per `SyncManager::new` (sync/core.rs:62).\n\n(d) THE DEFECT. `maybe_auto_hydrate` (hydration.rs:1184-1220) is called from `get_db()` on EVERY crosslink command (main.rs:2289-2294). It compares `hub_head_ref` = `git rev-parse HEAD` **in the hub-cache worktree** (hydration.rs:1234-1251) against `.crosslink/.last-hydrated-ref`, and on mismatch calls `hydrate_to_sqlite` unconditionally — no `hub_mode().is_v3()` gate. On a v3 hub whose cache worktree still hosts the v2 branch, that silently re-imports the stale v2 projection over the correct v3-derived DB.\nDamage model: `hydrate_to_sqlite`'s SQLite-only preservation keeps ONLY rows with `created_by IS NULL` (hydration.rs:166-178). ASES main DB: 218 rows, 0 with `created_by IS NULL` -> 100% of agent-authored issues dropped, leaving exactly the 4 June-era files. (The doc comment at hydration.rs:115-117 promises a \"significantly fewer issues => skip\" #427 guard; the code implements only the empty-`issue_files` early return at hydration.rs:126-128. Doc overstates the guard.)\n\nLIVE PROOF, reproduced twice IN THIS SESSION (not inference):\n- ASES hub-cache HEAD = `refs/heads/crosslink/hub`; `.hub-cache/issues/` = the 4 June UUID files (55991f4c/56547c9d/c8097b1a/f4919301); `.hub-cache/meta/counters.json` = `next_display_id: 5`.\n- `refs/heads/crosslink/hub` tip observed advancing eb6e4bf (05:30:52, \"trust: register signing key for 'pp3g-H4RK-...'\") -> 27361dc (05:39:26, \"trust: register signing key for 'yUNV-tmCJ-...'\"). The v2 branch is written continuously by unrelated agents' key registration.\n- At 05:41 and again at 05:44, `crosslink issue comment 142 ...` from this worktree failed with `Issue #142 not found`. The following `crosslink sync` printed `hydration: 4 local-only issue(s) collide with hub-assigned display id(s) [1, 2, 3, 4]; remapped to negative local ids` and re-hydrated 220 issues from the v3 refs. Post-recovery DB now permanently carries the 4 June issues as ids -1..-4 (preserved forever by `hydrate_from_state`'s SQLite-only rule, hydration.rs:350-367) — that is catalog 2.5 (display-id collisions), mechanically explained.\nCausal chain (complete): any agent's first sync -> trust commit on the checked-out v2 branch -> hub-cache HEAD moves -> `.last-hydrated-ref` stale in EVERY .crosslink dir (main repo + all worktrees; the marker is per-crosslink-dir but the HEAD is the SHARED main-repo cache, sync/core.rs:49-54) -> next crosslink command anywhere -> `maybe_auto_hydrate` -> June-era wipe. This also explains catalog 2.2 (\"mid-session drops on concurrent kickoff launches\"): a launch creates an agent, which registers a key, which moves the branch.\n\n== Q2: WHAT CONFIG KNOBS CONTROL THE HYDRATION SOURCE? ==\nEssentially NONE. There is no config key that selects hub vs checkpoint vs refs.\n- `tracker_remote` (hook-config.json; `sync::read_tracker_remote`, sync/mod.rs:68; registry entry config_registry.rs:128) selects only WHICH REMOTE is fetched (`fetch_and_adopt_v3_refs`, sync/cache.rs:398-405). It cannot redirect the local read.\n- `repo-alias.<name>` (config_registry.rs:170; `external::read_repo_alias`, external.rs:85-102) is for EXTERNAL cross-repo issue references only. Zero effect on hydration. (Rule out this hypothesis.)\n- There is no \"checkpoint setting\". Every ref name and path is a compile-time constant: `AGENT_REF_PREFIX`/`CHECKPOINT_REF`/`META_REF` (hub_v3.rs:37/45/49), `HUB_CACHE_DIR`=\".hub-cache\", `HUB_BRANCH`=\"crosslink/hub\", `HUB_V3_HOST_BRANCH`=\"crosslink/hub-v3-host\" (sync/mod.rs:17/22/29).\n- The cache location is not configurable either: always `<main repo root>/.crosslink/.hub-cache`, resolved through `resolve_main_repo_root` so worktrees share one cache (sync/core.rs:49-54).\n=> The real \"knobs\" are on-disk STATE, not config: (1) which refs exist (decides HubMode), (2) which branch the hub-cache worktree has checked out (decides what the v2 file path sees), (3) the `.crosslink/.last-hydrated-ref` marker (decides when auto-hydrate fires).\n\n== Q3: WHY IS THE HUB-CACHE ON THE WRONG REF — DEFECT OR OPERATOR STATE? ==\nDEFECT (init/sync), on top of legacy state. No operator ever checked that branch out.\n1. `SyncManager::init_cache` (sync/cache.rs:166-235) picks the worktree host with V2-FIRST precedence: `has_remote_v2 || has_local_v2` -> `init_v2_worktree` -> `git worktree add <cache> crosslink/hub` (sync/cache.rs:240-258). It never consults the v3 marker refs first — the exact opposite of `classify_hub_version`, where v3 wins when meta+checkpoint exist (hub_v3.rs:659-673). So any repo that has BOTH a legacy `crosslink/hub` branch and a live v3 hub gets its cache hosted on the v2 branch each time the cache is created.\n2. `init_cache` early-returns when the directory exists (sync/cache.rs:170-172). The host branch is never re-evaluated or corrected once wrong.\n3. Migration deliberately keeps the v2 branch: Phase A leaves `crosslink/hub` untouched and never re-hosts the cache (migrate_hub_v3.rs:115-123); only Phase B `--finalize --yes-delete-v2` removes the worktree and deletes the branch (migrate_hub_v3.rs:1427+, 1504-1540).\n4. ASES specifically was NEVER migrated: `refs/heads/crosslink/meta:hub.json` = `{\"hub_version\":3,\"migrated_from_commit\":\"genesis\",\"migrated_at\":\"2026-06-22T02:54:37Z\"}` — `\"genesis\"` is the fresh-bootstrap placeholder written by `bootstrap_v3_hub` (hub_v3.rs:1816). A fresh v3 hub was bootstrapped ALONGSIDE a pre-existing v2 branch. That is why the v2 reduced `issues/` projection was frozen at 4 June-era files and never advanced (catalog 2.9 explained: nothing was ever migrated into it, and v3 never writes it).\n5. AGGRAVATOR that turns a dormant stale checkout into a repeating trigger: the trust write path commits into the CHECKED-OUT branch with a plain `git commit` in the cache dir — `ensure_agent_key_published` (sync/trust.rs:391-403) and `commit_allowed_signers_unsigned` (sync/trust.rs:588-621, invoked from `configure_signing`/`register_active_key_as_trusted`, trust.rs:499-560). Both run on EVERY v3 sync (locks_cmd.rs:252-259). On a v3 hub these commits land on `crosslink/hub` even though the v3 read path takes its trust store from META_REF (`extract_meta_allowed_signers`, hub_source.rs:483-486, 589-606). Result: the v2 branch tip moves constantly, which is what fires the marker mismatch.\n6. TRAP for repairs: `crosslink/hub-v3-host` is NOT a clean orphan in ASES — `git ls-tree crosslink/hub-v3-host:issues` lists the SAME 4 stale files. Re-hosting the worktree onto it would NOT remove the stale projection.\n\n== Q4: DOES `crosslink integrity hydration --repair` READ THE SAME SOURCE? ==\nOn a v3 hub: YES, identical. `check_hydration` (integrity_cmd.rs:251) -> `v3_reduced_state` (integrity_cmd.rs:124-134) gates on `SyncManager::hub_mode().is_v3()`, builds `RefHubSource::new(cache_dir)` + `compaction::reduce`, and the repair calls `hydrate_from_state` (integrity_cmd.rs:335-336) — the same refs and the same reducer `crosslink sync` uses (locks_cmd.rs:263-265). Drift detection also takes the v3 state (integrity_cmd.rs:278). It snapshots the DB first (integrity_cmd.rs:305-313) and refuses unrecoverable loss without `--accept-data-loss` (integrity_cmd.rs:319-328).\nOn a NON-v3 hub: NO, and it is more dangerous than plain hydration. It runs `db.clear_shared_data()` and THEN `hydrate_to_sqlite(&cache_dir, db)` (integrity_cmd.rs:378-379). Because the clear happens OUTSIDE `hydrate_to_sqlite`, that function's SQLite-only snapshot (hydration.rs:141-190) sees an already-empty table and preserves nothing; if `issues/` is empty it early-returns (hydration.rs:126-128) leaving the DB wiped.\nCAVEAT: `check_hydration` derives `cache_dir` as `crosslink_dir.join(HUB_CACHE_DIR)` (integrity_cmd.rs:257) instead of `SyncManager::cache_path()`. Inside a linked worktree that path does not exist, so the check reports Skipped(\"sync not configured\"). Run integrity from the MAIN repo.\n\n== RECOMMENDED SAFE REPAIR PATH ==\nRanked. Config knob is NOT an option (none exists).\n1. IMMEDIATE, minimal, reversible, no refs touched (operator, main repo): remove the stale reduced projection from the hub-cache WORKING DIRECTORY so the v2 file path has nothing to import —\n   `rm -rf /home/claude-code/projects/ASES/.crosslink/.hub-cache/issues`\n   Effect: `read_all_issue_files` returns empty for a missing dir (issue_file.rs:225-230) -> `hydrate_to_sqlite` early-returns (hydration.rs:126-128) -> `maybe_auto_hydrate` degrades to a harmless marker refresh. No commit, no ref update, no push. Fully reversible with `git -C .crosslink/.hub-cache checkout -- issues` (the files stay in the branch tree and the index; the trust commits use `git add trust/...` + `git commit`, which commit the index and do not restore working files). The only path that could re-materialize them is `fetch_v2_readonly`'s `reset --hard` (sync/cache.rs:328-357), which is unreachable while the hub is v3 (locks_cmd.rs:246, cache.rs:305). Restore the dir before ever running `migrate hub-v3 --remigrate-from-v2`, which reads those files (`build_genesis_from_files`).\n   Do NOT instead re-host the worktree onto `crosslink/hub-v3-host` — same 4 stale files (see Q3.6).\n2. DO NOT run `crosslink migrate hub-v3 --finalize --yes-delete-v2` on ASES: it will refuse, by design. `compute_v2_divergence` (migrate_hub_v3.rs:1784-1802) + `is_stale` (1718-1721): with `migrated_from_commit == \"genesis\"`, `git rev-list --count genesis..<tip>` fails -> `commits_ahead = None` -> stale -> `bail!` (migrate_hub_v3.rs:1458-1470). Even past that, the AC-6 re-verify `verify_against_files` (migrate_hub_v3.rs:1118-1153) compares 4 files against ~220 reduced issues and fails. Finalize is not a usable repair here.\n3. AFTER a wipe has already happened: `crosslink sync` alone restores the DB from the v3 refs (observed twice today: 218 then 220 issues). `crosslink compact` + `crosslink sync` (playbook §6.5) remains the belt-and-braces path; both use RefHubSource -> `hydrate_from_state` (compact.rs:46-48; locks_cmd.rs:263-265). Expect the 4 June issues to persist as negative ids — cosmetic, and they are the reason display ids can appear reassigned.\n4. PERMANENT CODE FIX (fork PR; feeds #125/#157), in priority order:\n   (i) Gate `maybe_auto_hydrate` on hub mode (hydration.rs:1184): when `sync.hub_mode().is_v3()`, either skip or route through `RefHubSource` + `hydrate_from_state`. This single change removes the rollback trigger.\n   (ii) Key the freshness marker on the hub DATA refs (checkpoint tip) instead of the cache worktree HEAD (`hub_head_ref`, hydration.rs:1234-1251) — HEAD tracks a branch v3 does not read.\n   (iii) Route trust writes to META_REF via `hub_v3::commit_blob_to_ref` rather than committing into the checked-out branch (sync/trust.rs:391-403, 588-621), so no v3 operation ever moves `crosslink/hub`.\n   (iv) Make `init_cache` consult `detect_hub_version` BEFORE the v2-first branch and re-host an existing cache when the hub is v3 (sync/cache.rs:166-185, 170-172).\n   (v) Make the non-v3 `integrity hydration --repair` stop clearing outside `hydrate_to_sqlite` (integrity_cmd.rs:378-379), and use `SyncManager::cache_path()` for `cache_dir` (integrity_cmd.rs:257).\n\n== SCOPE / HONESTY ==\nRead-only task: no file in /home/claude-code/projects/crosslink or ASES was modified, no commit, no push, and no mutating crosslink command beyond the mandated `sync`/comment calls. The two `Issue #142 not found` failures at 05:41/05:44 were unsolicited live reproductions of the failure under investigation, not induced experiments. Catalog cross-refs: 2.1 (June-era rollback — mechanism now fully explained), 2.2 (concurrent-kickoff drops — same trigger), 2.5 (display-id collisions — the negative-id remap), 2.9 (frozen 4-file projection — explained by fresh v3 bootstrap alongside an unmigrated v2 branch). Issue #142 is NOT closed.","created_at":"2026-08-06T05:45:50.932033035Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:1+ojUpN/l2A/OQ2qE+3qjzFKHPIB7X6Z0gGIrE1ryMU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg46kUx2n/iKXFTA2LAjlpaWMncRtHBl22/+W7gnHpDvwAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAo70q3+g7+vi0CMiuAlCCqAmho6uRs/mIb84PI5GeN8z7ujkfCGAoKJrkPLRGL4Pi670yh3gfRH3GATJTaCFUCg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:1+ojUpN/l2A/OQ2qE+3qjzFKHPIB7X6Z0gGIrE1ryMU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg46kUx2n/iKXFTA2LAjlpaWMncRtHBl22/+W7gnHpDvwAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAAB